---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { db } from "../lib/db.js";
import { getLeagues, getSummary } from "../lib/queries.js";

const leagues = getLeagues(db);
const s = getSummary(db);
---

<Base title="How it works">
  <h1>How Atlas XI works</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Atlas XI scouts footballers who could still choose to play for <strong>Morocco</strong> — and ranks
    them with a rating built to be fair across leagues. Here's what that means.
  </p>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Who's on this list</h2>
    <p>
      Every player here is <strong>eligible for Morocco but not yet tied to its senior team</strong
      >. A player with two nationalities can freely choose a country — until he plays one
      competitive match for a senior national team, which locks him to it for good (that appearance
      is called a <em>cap</em>).
    </p>
    <ul class="statuses">
      <li>
        <span class="badge eligible">eligible</span> Moroccan by nationality or descent, with{" "}
        <strong>0 senior caps</strong> — free to be recruited. Youth caps (U-17 → U-23) don't count, so
        a player who's featured for a Morocco or another country's youth team is still here.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="badge review">review</span> Moroccan-eligible but has already played a senior match
        for{" "}
        <strong>another country</strong>. Often still switchable (friendlies don't tie a player), so
        we flag rather than hide them — worth a manual check.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="badge excluded">excluded</span> Not shown: already a Morocco senior international
        (job done), or committed elsewhere.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>The fair score</h2>
    <p>
      A raw match rating (like SofaScore's) has two blind spots: it ignores <strong>how long</strong
      > a player was on the pitch and <strong>how strong</strong> his league is. A striker who scores
      in a 10-minute cameo can post an 8.0; a defender who's solid for 90 minutes gets a 7.0. The cameo
      isn't better. Our score fixes that in three steps:
    </p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><b>Weight by minutes.</b> A rating over 90 minutes counts far more than one over 10.</li>
      <li>
        <b>Trust the sample.</b> With few minutes played, the score is pulled toward an average baseline
        — you have to earn the minutes before a big number sticks. This is what stops the cameo from topping
        the list.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Adjust for league strength.</b> The result is multiplied by a league coefficient, so a 7.0
        in the Premier League outranks a 7.0 in a weaker division.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="egbox">
      <b>Worked example.</b> An 8.0 across 50 minutes all season scores <b>6.82</b>; a 7.0 across
      2700 minutes scores <b>6.95</b>. The steady starter correctly comes out on top.
    </p>
    <p class="fine">
      Only <strong>league matches</strong> count (cups and internationals are excluded). A player needs{
        " "
      }
      <strong>450+ league minutes</strong> to make the Best XI. Scores sit lower than raw ratings because
      of the league multiplier and the pull toward baseline — that's expected, and it's what makes them
      comparable.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>League strength</h2>
    <p>Hand-set starting coefficients (1.00 = strongest). Every match is weighted by its league:</p>
    <div class="coeffs">
      {
        leagues.map((l) => (
          <div class="coeff">
            <span>{l.name}</span>
            <b>{l.coefficient.toFixed(2)}</b>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Glossary</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>Score</dt>
      <dd>
        Our fair rating: minutes-weighted, sample-adjusted, league-weighted. The number we rank by.
      </dd>
      <dt>Rating</dt>
      <dd>
        The raw average match rating, for reference. Score is Rating made comparable across leagues.
      </dd>
      <dt>Mins / Apps</dt>
      <dd>
        League minutes played and appearances this season — how large the sample behind the score
        is.
      </dd>
      <dt>Positions</dt>
      <dd>
        GK goalkeeper · CB centre-back · FB full-back · DM/CM/AM midfield · W winger · ST striker.
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <p class="src">
    Covering {s.eligible} eligible players across {leagues.length} divisions. Data: Transfermarkt (eligibility)
    · SofaScore (match ratings & minutes). Season 2025/26.
  </p>

  <style>
    .card {
      background: var(--card);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 14px;
      padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }
    .card h2 {
      margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
      font-size: 1.15rem;
    }
    .card p {
      margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
    }
    .statuses {
      list-style: none;
      padding: 0;
      margin: 0;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.7rem;
    }
    .statuses li {
      font-size: 0.92rem;
    }
    .badge {
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
      border-radius: 999px;
      text-transform: capitalize;
      margin-right: 0.35rem;
    }
    .badge.eligible {
      background: rgba(0, 98, 51, 0.15);
      color: var(--green);
    }
    .badge.review {
      background: rgba(193, 39, 45, 0.13);
      color: var(--red);
    }
    .badge.excluded {
      background: var(--border);
      color: var(--muted);
    }
    .steps {
      margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
      padding-left: 1.2rem;
    }
    .steps li {
      margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    }
    .egbox {
      background: rgba(0, 98, 51, 0.08);
      border-left: 3px solid var(--green);
      padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem;
      border-radius: 6px;
      font-size: 0.92rem;
    }
    .fine {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
    }
    .coeffs {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(190px, 1fr));
      gap: 0.4rem;
    }
    .coeff {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      padding: 0.35rem 0.6rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 8px;
      font-size: 0.88rem;
    }
    .coeff b {
      color: var(--green);
    }
    dl {
      margin: 0;
    }
    dt {
      font-weight: 800;
      margin-top: 0.6rem;
    }
    dd {
      margin: 0.1rem 0 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.92rem;
    }
    .src {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.82rem;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
